# BusyBox init: set up the system once, then keep a login shell on the serial console. Naming a device in the first
# field makes init open it as the shell's controlling terminal, so Ctrl-C and job control work; "console" is /dev/console,
# which always exists (a static node in the image) and is redirected by the kernel to the real console. (Naming
# ttyLXU0 did not work on the board: that node was not there.)
::sysinit:/etc/init.d/rcS
console::respawn:-/bin/sh
::ctrlaltdel:/sbin/reboot
::shutdown:/bin/umount -a -r
